#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:17
#: 249af99753f14300a3888e50f781dedb
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:19
#: b96e69ebe318487099977870272bfd0a
msgid "This manual is fairly self-contained and covers all instructions necessary for setting up X-Plane and ArduPilot's SITL, getting them to talk to each other, and having ArduPlane fly an RC sailplane through X-Plane's soaring missions. Links to all requisite extras such as RC sailplane models for X-Plane, parameters files, and other potentially useful material are included in the document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:21
#: b926592a72e24da9b45de0319c844828
msgid "The instructions have been tested on Windows 8.1 and 10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:26
#: 11ea8c5644504299bc8db8d7fe2d9775
msgid "Setting up X-Plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:28
#: 92e480e0a4c941a8a2a8fb3c3bb92b9e
msgid "**Download the** `X-Plane 10 demo <http://www.x-plane.com/desktop/try-it/older/>`_ **or buy the full version.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:30
#: fcba501d8cc8476a8e4ee05982217457
msgid "X-Plane 11 also works, but the instructions below assume X-Plane 10's UI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:33
#: 22b7dfc849f34ef0a58738541b64d547
msgid "The demo version will prevent you from controlling the plane manually after 15 minutes of flying or so, but flying in ArduPlane modes that don’t require manual input, e.g., Auto, and switching modes from a ground control station such as :ref:`Mission Planner <mission-planner-overview>` will work even after that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:38
#: 275af7058202430fa48a2cb0191e70bb
msgid "**Configure a joystick/transmitter for use with X-Plane.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:40
#: a6c362b197c44807979424c95d29eaa7
msgid "X-Plane requires a joystick for manually controlling yaw, pitch, and roll. However, several transmitters for RC aircraft, e.g., FrSky Taranis, can also be used as joysticks for X-Plane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:42
#: 74ecb04bbc83490d8b90cd215330368e
msgid "To use an FrSky Taranis as an X-Plane joystick:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:44
#: 446a39bfd5e746beb2017d693a960a38
msgid "Switch on the Taranis, connect it to your PC with a mini USB cable, and move its On-Off switch to Off. The Taranis will stay on without using its battery -- it is now getting power from the PC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:46
#: c08812ef3dd54e8ebf4f85df38adc8f4
msgid "Calibrate it (this needs to be done only the first time you use it as your joystick). You can do so in Windows (on Windows 10: *Start menu -> Settings -> Devices -> Printers and Scanners -> Devices and Printers*) or in X-Plane (start X-Plane, hover near the top of the X-Plane window, and in the toolbar at that appears at the top of the window go to *Settings -> Joystick & Equipment*). For more info on joystick calibration in X-Plane, please refer to the `Setup of X-Plane 10 <https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/sitl-with-xplane.html#setup-of-x-plane-10>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:49
#: 6013215ffe2c448f951f6ee79f46f367
msgid "This setup allows you to control throttle, yaw, pitch, and roll. Other commands, such as switching modes, will have to be issued via Mission Planner or some other means."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:53
#: 40c10b88ff074a1ca29ca840865b4f8f
msgid "**Install RC sailplane models and airfoils for them into X-Plane.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:55
#: 038f8b532acc408ea30dcc19a462f3d0
msgid "By default, X-Plane has no models of RC sailplanes' size (~5-meter wingspan), weight (a few kilos), or flying characteristics. However, generous folks have created and published some:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:57
#: 17f375d0e349442ca26810d140f41f76
msgid "`Vee-gull 005 <http://www.scipie.com/rc/vee-gull/vee-gull_005.zip>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:58
#: 4c662c05b8ea4989ae6561f725e12836
msgid "`Houston Hawk <http://wkleinsasser.net/download/Houston_Hawk_Xplane.zip>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:59
#: 64e2d48ebe0a400c94e9400408cf12a3
msgid "`Viking 74 <http://wkleinsasser.net/download/Viking_74.zip>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:60
#: 63cee42517da4a99b7b8acf403610151
msgid "`Vivace 100 <http://wkleinsasser.net/download/Vivace_100_Xplane.zip>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:61
#: 98aa86cf846048c695d82189c6f379ca
msgid "`Vivace 126 <http://wkleinsasser.net/download/Vivace_126_Xplane.zip>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:63
#: fc34ac51b679446194ca16d879d292d1
msgid "To install them, create a folder *RC Sailplanes* under *%XPlane-install-dir%\\\\Aircraft* and extract the .acf files from these archives there. `Extra info on sailplane model installation is here <http://wkleinsasser.net/download/x-plane_glider_model_directions.pdf>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:65
#: 5d1e864a98e3413aa6d60e7ed143c32e
msgid "Unfortunately, the X-Plane 10 demo doesn’t provide airfoils for most of the above models, and refuses to load these models without them. Fortunately, someone has created and published the airfoils too!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:67
#: 99c633551d6e4268aa39e77523b363b0
msgid "The airfoils are in `NACA_64_xxx_Airfoils_from_TR824.zip in the ArduPilot repo <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/Tools/Frame_params/XPlane>`_. Originally, this archive comes from `a post on X-Plane forum <http://forums.x-plane.org/index.php?/files/file/6953-several-naca-64-series-airfoils/>`_, and `this X-Plane forum thread <http://forums.x-plane.org/index.php?/files/category/3-airfoils/>`_ is a good place to look for more airfoils."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:69
#: 7fefa60d813e4622869064b28ad92f93
msgid "To install them, extract the .afl files from the downloaded archive into *%XPlane-install-dir%\\\\Airfoils*.  This will enable you to fly, at the very least, Vee-gull 005 and Houston Hawk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/soaring-sitl-with-xplane.rst:73
#: 031e875e000a47cc8b092f155e31a3fb
msgid "**Configure X-Plane for communicating with ArduPilot.**"
msgstr ""

